      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "## Bevy version\r\n`0.12`\r\n\r\n## What you did\r\n\r\n```rust\r\nuse bevy::prelude::*;\r\n\r\nfn main() {\r\n    App::new()\r\n        .add_plugins(DefaultPlugins)\r\n        .add_systems(Update, hide_cursor)\r\n        .run();\r\n}\r\n\r\nfn hide_cursor(\r\n    mut windows: Query<&mut Window>,\r\n    mouse: Res<Input<MouseButton>>,\r\n    key: Res<Input<KeyCode>>,\r\n) {\r\n    let mut window = windows.single_mut();\r\n\r\n    if mouse.just_pressed(MouseButton::Left) {\r\n        window.cursor.visible = false;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    if key.just_pressed(KeyCode::Escape) {\r\n        window.cursor.visible = true;\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n## What went wrong\r\n\r\n- What were you expecting?\r\nThe cursor becomes hidden.\r\n\r\n- What actually happened?\r\nThe cursor is not hidden\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThe cursor is correctly hidden in the desktop builds.\r\n\r\nWhen you grab the cursor with:\r\n\r\n```rust\r\nwindow.cursor.grab_mode = CursorGrabMode::Locked;\r\n```\r\n\r\nCursor hiding will work in the web build.\r\n\r\nYou can get around this issue by setting `cursor: none;` in the CSS, so at the very least there should be some sort of API to control this.\r\n",
